---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ActionLink from "../../../../components/ActionLink.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Icon from "../../../../components/Icon.astro";
import MarkdownH1 from "../../../../components/MarkdownH1.astro";
import MarkdownH2 from "../../../../components/MarkdownH2.astro";
import MarkdownList from "../../../../components/MarkdownList.astro";
import Prose from "../../../../components/Prose.astro";
import TerminalCommands from "../../../../components/TerminalCommands.astro";

import { opencodeInspector } from "../../../../config/opencode-inspector";
import { projectLinks } from "../../../../config/site";

const source = `${projectLinks.github}/tree/main/integrations/opencode/panel`;
const pluginConfig = `{
	"plugins": [
		{
			"package": "${opencodeInspector.package}",
			"options": {
				"rows": 2,
				"current": "glyph"
			}
		}
	]
}`;
---

<BaseLayout title={`${opencodeInspector.title} for OpenCode | Zinn`} description={opencodeInspector.description}>
	<div class='site-container py-8 md:py-12'>
		<Breadcrumbs
			items={[
				{ name: "Integrations", path: "/integrations/" },
				{ name: "OpenCode task inspector", path: Astro.url.pathname }
			]}
		/>

		<section class='pb-9 md:pb-12'>
			<MarkdownH1>{opencodeInspector.title}</MarkdownH1>
			<div class='grid gap-7 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_1fr] md:items-end md:gap-12'>
				<p class='max-w-md text-lg leading-relaxed'>Experimental. {opencodeInspector.description}</p>
				<div class='flex flex-wrap gap-3 md:justify-end'>
					<ActionLink href='#installation'>Installation</ActionLink>
					<ActionLink href={source} variant='outline'>Source</ActionLink>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<div class='max-w-3xl'>
			<Prose>
				<p>
					The inspector reads tasks, labels and recorded activity through the local Zinn CLI. It uses the same <a
						href='/docs/settings'>data directory and settings</a
					> as the CLI running in that environment. It loads active tasks from the default project, or from every project
					when no default is set. With a remote OpenCode server, the inspector still runs locally and reads the local CLI's
					database.
				</p>

				<MarkdownH2>Requirements</MarkdownH2>
				<MarkdownList>
					<li>OpenCode {opencodeInspector.verifiedVersion}.</li>
					<li>
						Zinn CLI {opencodeInspector.minimumCliVersion} or newer on the terminal's <code>PATH</code>, with a database
						it can read.
					</li>
					<li>The inspector package <code>{opencodeInspector.package}</code>.</li>
				</MarkdownList>

				<MarkdownH2 id='installation'>Install</MarkdownH2>
				<p>
					Add the package to <code>~/.config/opencode/cli.json</code>, keeping any existing plugin entries:
				</p>
				<TerminalCommands label='OpenCode plugin configuration' commands={[pluginConfig]} showsPrompt={false} />
				<p>
					OpenCode loads this TUI-only package through its native <a href='https://opencode.ai/v2/docs/cli/plugins/'
						>CLI plugin configuration</a
					>. Start OpenCode, open a conversation and mention a task key from your database. Select the task to inspect
					it.
				</p>

				<MarkdownH2>Find and inspect tasks</MarkdownH2>
				<p>
					Run <code>/zinn</code> to find a loaded active task. The command palette also offers{" "}
					<strong>Zinn: task keys in this chat</strong> and{" "}
					<strong>Zinn: pick a task from the board</strong>.
				</p>
				<p>
					Task details include status, priority, labels, relations, comment count and the first paragraph of the
					description. Unknown keys are shown when their project prefix appears among the loaded tasks. Select the ZINN
					heading to refresh task and label data.
				</p>

				<MarkdownH2>Options</MarkdownH2>
				<dl class='my-6 space-y-5'>
					<div>
						<dt class='font-mono font-semibold'>rows</dt>
						<dd class='mt-1'>
							Values <code>1</code> and <code>2</code>, default <code>1</code>. <code>2</code> includes column, priority and
							labels.
						</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt class='font-mono font-semibold'>current</dt>
						<dd class='mt-1'>
							Values <code>"off"</code> and <code>"glyph"</code>, default <code>"off"</code>.
							<code>"glyph"</code> marks tasks with recorded activity from this conversation family.
						</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>

				<MarkdownH2>Conversation marks</MarkdownH2>
				<p>
					A conversation mark means a task has recorded activity whose session or thread ID matches the current
					conversation, its root or one of its children. A mention alone does not create a mark. The mark records
					activity, rather than an assignment or ownership claim.
				</p>
				<p>
					OpenCode's native shell session ID is recorded by Zinn as a thread ID. An explicit
					<code>ZINN_SESSION_ID</code> and <code>ZINN_THREAD_ID</code> pair takes precedence. The inspector recognizes both
					routes. See <a href='/docs/cli#who-am-i'>actor identity</a> for the CLI contract.
				</p>
				<p>
					The mark animates while OpenCode reports that conversation as busy. Busy state comes from the host
					independently of the task's recorded activity. Tasks in Done keep their green treatment.
				</p>

				<MarkdownH2>Compatibility</MarkdownH2>
				<p>
					Version {opencodeInspector.version} targets OpenCode {opencodeInspector.verifiedVersion} and its OpenTUI 0.7.0 runtime.
					Keep the inspector's version pinned when updating OpenCode and check the inspector's compatibility guidance before
					adopting a new host release.
				</p>

				<MarkdownH2>Update</MarkdownH2>
				<p>
					Replace the version in the package entry with the compatible inspector version you want, then start OpenCode
					again. OpenCode manages the package download. Keep your existing options in the entry.
				</p>

				<MarkdownH2>Remove</MarkdownH2>
				<p>
					Remove the <code>{opencodeInspector.packageName}</code> entry from <code>cli.json</code>, then start OpenCode
					again. Your Zinn projects, tasks and activity remain in the database.
				</p>
			</Prose>

			<div class='mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-5 border-t border-pewter pt-6'>
				<p class='font-mono text-xs'>Verified with OpenCode {opencodeInspector.verifiedVersion}</p>
				<a class='inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs' href={source}
					>Inspector source <Icon name='external-link' /></a
				>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
